      <!-- Hiking Tips for Bangor Area -->
      <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50 to-blue-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-emerald-200">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-6">Essential Tips for Hiking Near Bangor</h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🚗</span> Getting There
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Acadia trailheads are reached via Route 1A and Route 3 toward Ellsworth and Mount Desert Island</li>
              <li>• Baxter State Park is north via I-95 and Millinocket; the final miles into the park are on park roads</li>
              <li>• Acadia requires an entrance pass and Baxter manages day-use parking — check NPS and Baxter State Park for current rules</li>
              <li>• Download offline maps; cell service drops quickly in the mountains</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🎒</span> What to Bring
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Sturdy shoes — Acadia's granite ledges and iron rungs are slick when wet</li>
              <li>• Water and food for a longer day than you planned</li>
              <li>• Layers and a wind shell — alpine weather changes fast</li>
              <li>• Headlamp and a first aid kit</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">📅</span> Best Times to Visit
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• <strong>Summer (Jun-Aug):</strong> Warm and busy on the coast; Katahdin's upper routes are best from midsummer on</li>
              <li>• <strong>Early fall (Sep):</strong> Cooler, fewer crowds, fall color — daylight shrinks fast</li>
              <li>• <strong>Winter (Nov-Apr):</strong> Ice and deep snow on the high routes — only with proper skills and gear</li>
              <li>• <strong>Spring (Apr-May):</strong> Mud season: snowmelt and soft trails, and some park roads and trailheads stay closed</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">⚠️</span> Safety First
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Check the forecast and trail conditions before leaving</li>
              <li>• Tell someone your hiking plans</li>
              <li>• Turn back if weather deteriorates</li>
              <li>• Stay on marked trails; some Acadia routes close seasonally for nesting peregrine falcons</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
